# Welcome

This is the documentation for **{{projectName}}** — a full-stack web application built with React + FastAPI, scaffolded with [`dude`](https://github.com/cubocicloide/dude).

---

## Getting started

`dude` is the project CLI, published on the public npm registry. Install the
global launcher, then provision and start the app.

```bash
# 1. Install the dude launcher globally (the only global install).
npm install -g @cubocicloide/dude-launcher

# 2. Scaffold the project (how {{projectName}} was created). Already inside it
#    or cloned it? Skip this and go straight to `pnpm install`.
dude init {{projectName}}
cd {{projectName}}

# 3. Provision the project's pinned toolchain (CLI + stack) from the lockfile.
pnpm install

# 4. Build the images and start every service (first run).
dude up
{{#if withPostgres}}

# 5. Apply migrations and seed demo data (first run only — see below).
dude reset
{{/if}}
```

From then on, `dude up` starts everything and `dude down` stops it. See
[Working with dude](dude.md) for the full command reference and
[the README](https://github.com/cubocicloide/dude) for prerequisites.
{{#if withPostgres}}

!!! tip "First run with PostgreSQL"
    The backend applies pending Alembic migrations automatically on every
    `dude up`, so the schema is always in sync — but a brand-new database has
    no data in it. Run `dude reset` once after the first `dude up` to drop the
    database, re-apply migrations, and seed demo users; otherwise pages like
    **Users** simply render empty until you create data yourself.
{{/if}}

To serve this documentation site:

```bash
dude docs          # → http://localhost:8001
```

!!! info "Extending this site"
    This site is served straight from `docs/docs/` — add or edit Markdown
    files there and `dude docs` picks them up on save. See
    [Writing docs](mkdocs.md) for the supported syntax and how to add pages.

